WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:11.210
37. Cyberbullying. With the Internet, our friends are nearby even when they aren't.

2
00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:19.210
Unfortunately, while the Internet allows us to stay close to our friends, it can also make us more vulnerable to our enemies.

3
00:00:19.210 --> 00:00:27.210
Bullying has always been a problem in schools. Big kids pick on smaller kids, rich kids make fun of poor kids.

4
00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:32.210
But nowadays, kids are being bullied even at home, where they should be safe.

5
00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:38.210
Cyberbullying, which means bullying people over the Internet, is a serious and growing problem.

6
00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:46.210
And since the Internet is always on and always available, victims of cyberbullying can feel like nowhere is safe.

7
00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:51.210
Cyberbullying often occurs on social media sites like Facebook and Twitter.

8
00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:57.210
Bullies post cruel comments on their victims' pages or send them mocking or threatening messages.

9
00:00:58.210 --> 00:01:03.210
Rumors spread quickly online, so it can be hard for victims to defend themselves.

10
00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:06.210
Sometimes other people join in on the attacks.

11
00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:11.210
People seem to be more willing to join in attacks online than they would be in person.

12
00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:16.210
In the end, victims can feel as if their whole class or school has turned against them.

13
00:01:16.210 --> 00:01:19.210
It's a very lonely and frightening feeling.

14
00:01:19.210 --> 00:01:25.210
Studies show that over half of U.S. school kids have experienced bullying online.

15
00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:29.210
Just one in ten of them will tell his or her parents about it.

16
00:01:29.210 --> 00:01:33.210
And less than 20 percent of these incidents will be reported to the police.

17
00:01:33.210 --> 00:01:36.210
Cyberbullying is very dangerous.

18
00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:41.210
There have been several instances of teenagers committing suicide because of it.

19
00:01:41.210 --> 00:01:47.210
It is also largely invisible, which makes it hard to identify and even harder to stop.

20
00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:50.210
Many countries have passed laws against cyberbullying.

21
00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:54.210
Whether these laws will help end this crime for good remains to be seen.
